<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:56:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Meta continues to run ads promoting child sexual abuse material in India - report</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqxv2vwjjq3o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:27:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqxv2vwjjq3o--d39fb1c8e98b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqxv2vwjjq3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The report follows a BBC Eye investigation that found Instagram running paid ads promoting such material in India.</summary></entry><entry><title>Should promotion depend on how workers use AI?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1j1896e973o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:56:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:05:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1j1896e973o--ad6c061b96f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1j1896e973o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">More companies are tying career progression to AI use: is that fair?</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI says it cracked 90-year-old maths problem in 88 hours</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:56:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T20:57:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o--c539a0032086.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI's claim that it solved parts of Navier-Stokes equations has quickly stirred controversy.</summary></entry><entry><title>New law to force tech firms to stop children taking or sharing nude images</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgrv9ypp5x2o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:48:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgrv9ypp5x2o--6890aee9fa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgrv9ypp5x2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The government said it will legislate "as soon as they can" but may "reassess" its plans if firms make the desired changes sooner.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scammers demand ransoms from Instagram users over fake copyright claims</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjw54ww73qjo#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:49:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjw54ww73qjo--b4f2ac41fd12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjw54ww73qjo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Users say they are losing money or risk having their accounts suspended because Meta struggles to identify scammers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Grindr to pay £26m to settle claims it allegedly shared users' HIV status</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8e63qdqwzo#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:27:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8e63qdqwzo--9c5ec95b83db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn8e63qdqwzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The long-running claim alleges Grindr breached UK privacy laws by sharing data with third parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI chief scientist warns no-one is prepared for consequences of AI</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzrrd0kp7o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:22:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzrrd0kp7o--6ca44da74670.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwyzrrd0kp7o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The post comes as the firm releases GPT-6 Astra, which it says is its most powerful product yet.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dolly Parton's sister pleads for end to 'AI garbage' posts after singer's death</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1wxppnrqlqo#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T11:30:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1wxppnrqlqo--cb89067443e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1wxppnrqlqo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Since Parton's death in late August, dozens of AI-generated songs, images and videos have appeared online.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI agents hijacked German website before Hugging Face hack, report claims</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckg725z5kgzo#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:59:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckg725z5kgzo--4f5dd1d21115.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckg725z5kgzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI said it could not "meaningfully respond" to the report's findings because it hadn't been allowed to review it ahead of publication.</summary></entry><entry><title>Xbox caps cloud gaming at 15 hours a month for Game Pass subscribers</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj06zd4l99lo#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:48:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj06zd4l99lo--5f2a767e1e16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj06zd4l99lo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Xbox said the limits were due to the rising cost of cloud gaming, and would allow it to invest more in its performance</summary></entry><entry><title>Could robots be the future of theme parks?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cdr7g3vdl58o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T02:02:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cdr7g3vdl58o--17cf8c14f1b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cdr7g3vdl58o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Galaxy Robot Park is a 16,500-square-meter venue in South Korea, with attractions including humanoid robots dancing to K-pop hits.</summary></entry><entry><title>'I lost my savings after a job interview scam'</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crk3xd8j3k5o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T23:41:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crk3xd8j3k5o--14e89cd5510f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crk3xd8j3k5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Jobseekers, especially Gen Z, are being targeted with fake, booby-trapped recruitment apps.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI data centres are booming in Australia - but at what cost?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgl3we7wdr3o#0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T18